      "final_text": "Done. `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is fixed and all five required theorems are proved.\n\n**Fix** ([Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean:12)): `sqrt` is now the deployed loop with the v0.4.1 correction \u2014 the minimum of the last two iterates (`if y < z then y else z`) instead of always taking `z`. On raw `9999999998` this yields `9999999998` (the floor) rather than `9999999999`.\n\n**Proof sketch** (all in `namespace VyperSqrt`, core Lean only): with `N = a\u00b710\u00b9\u2070`, `s = Nat.sqrt N`, the Nat Newton step `F(z) = (N/z + z)/2` satisfies `F(z) \u2265 s` for all `z \u2265 1`, equals `s` at `s+1`, stays in `{s, s+1}` from `s`, strictly decreases above `s+1`, and at least halves the distance `z \u2212 s` there \u2014 so the tail reaches `{s, s+1}` within 167 of the 256 iterations. The Int `loop` is shown to follow these Nat iterates within range (so it never reverts), and its final minimum equals `s`, giving `r\u00b2 \u2264 x\u00b7D` and `x\u00b7D < (r+1)\u00b2`. Negative inputs revert and the deployed-loop shape holds by definition.\n\n**Verification**: `lake build Solution` succeeds with no `sorry`; only `candidate/Solution.lean` changed; no forbidden constructs; `#print axioms` shows at most `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`, matching the allowed set.",
